<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40992" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-lŏco</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v. a.
		(late Lat.) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To bring a thing back to its former place</i>, <i>to</i>
			
			
			<i>replace</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">linguam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 1, 4, 75</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">articulum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 1, 28</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To let out again</i>, <i>relet</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Dig. 19, 2, 13, § 10</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">19, 2, 51</span></i>
			praef.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
